invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_mul.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: p256_wide_base_mul never keeps the sum it corrected, so an even
  scalar k gives (k + 1) * G: the digits are those of k | 1. Every odd
  scalar is still right. bin/p256_equiv_test multiplies G by even
  scalars, 0, 2 and 16 among them and half of its random ones.

--- old
    p256_wide_point_add_affine(&corrected, &sum, &entry);
    point_cmov(&sum, &corrected, p256_wide_mask(scalar_bit(k, 0) ^ 1U));
--- new
    p256_wide_point_add_affine(&corrected, &sum, &entry);
    point_cmov(&sum, &corrected, 0);
